summary:
  One const returns to a callback on the General settings page and qmllint
  stops reading that page, without a word and with exit 0.

history:
  qmllint compiles a function that sits inside another one a second time,
  and a const or let in it fails that second time; the object it is in and
  every object after it are dropped (measured on 6.12.0, 2026-11-12).
  Fifty-one such declarations were turned into var on 2026-09-20. By
  2026.43 twelve had grown back and by 2026-11-12 seventeen, in
  FullRepresentation.qml, configGeneral.qml and configSearch.qml; the first
  and the last were unread from their first object on, this page from
  part-way down. This is one of the seventeen, put back.

target:
  package/contents/ui/config/configGeneral.qml

find:
                          var flat = {};

replace:
                          const flat = {};

expect:
  Killed by the lint's qmllint pass itself, scripts/qmllint_gate.py:
  "qmllint does not analyse ui/config/configGeneral.qml". No test stands
  behind this one on purpose: it is the shipped file going unread, and the
  pass is what has to notice. That the pass can notice at all is what
  tests/test_qmllint_gate.py::test_a_file_qmllint_gives_up_on_fails_by_name
  holds.
